calculate \\(x_8\\):\n\\[x_8 = x_7 - x_6 + x_5 - x_4 = -265 - (-101) + 267 - 523 = -420\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(x_9\\):\n\\[x_9 = x_8 - x_7 + x_6 - x_5 = -420 - (-265) + (-101) - 267 = -523\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(x_{10}\\):\n\\[x_{10} = x_9 - x_8 + x_7 - x_6 = -523 - (-420) + (-265) - (-101) = -267\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(x_{11}\\):\n\\[x_{11} = x_{10} - x_9 + x_8 - x_7 = -267 - (-523) + (-420) - (-265) = 101\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(x_{12}\\):\n\\[x_{12} = x_{11} - x_{10} + x_9 - x_8 = 101 - (-267) + (-523) - (-420) = 265\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(x_{13}\\):\n\\[x_{13} = x_{12} - x_{11} + x_{10} - x_9 = 265 - 101 + (-267) - (-523) = 420\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(x_{14}\\):\n\\[x_{14} = x_{13} - x_{12} + x_{11} - x_{10} = 420 - 265 + 101 - (-267) = 523\\]\n\nWe observe that \\(x_{13} = x_3\\) and \\(x_{14} = x_4\\). This indicates that the sequence repeats every 12 terms. Therefore, we can express any term \\(x_n\\) as \\(x_{n \\mod 12}\\).\n\nNow, we need to find \\(x_{531} + x_{753} + x_{975}\\):\n\\[531 \\mod 12 = 3 \\implies x_{531} = x_3 = 420\\]\n\\[753 \\mod 12 = 9 \\implies x_{753} = x_9 = -523\\]\n\\[975 \\mod 12 = 3 \\implies x_{975} = x_3 = 420\\]\n\nSo, we have:\n\\[x_{531} + x_{753} + x_{975} = 420 + (-523) + 420 = 317\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\\boxed{317}\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{317}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
